---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout 
  title="Privacy Policy | K&R Photography" 
  description="Privacy Policy for K&R Photography (Kimberly & Rick). Learn how we collect, protect, and handle your information for photography sessions and bookings."
>
  <div class="legal-page-header">
    <div class="legal-header-inner">
      <div class="legal-eyebrow">
        <span class="gold-line"></span>
        <span>Studio Governance</span>
        <span class="gold-line"></span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="legal-title">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="legal-meta">Effective Date: June 2024 · Last Updated: August 2026</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <main class="legal-body-container">
    <div class="legal-content">
      
      <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>1. Commitment to Your Privacy</h2>
        <p>
          At <strong>K&amp;R Photography</strong> ("we," "us," or "our," operated by Kimberly &amp; Rick), we value the trust you place in us when inviting us to capture your milestone events, weddings, family portraits, and real estate properties. This Privacy Policy outlines how we collect, use, and protect your personal information when you visit <strong>kandrpix.com</strong> or communicate with our studio.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>2. Information We Collect</h2>
        <p>We only collect personal information that you voluntarily provide to us when inquiring about or booking a photography session:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Contact Details:</strong> Full name, email address, phone number, and physical billing/mailing address.</li>
          <li><strong>Event &amp; Session Specifications:</strong> Requested event dates, ceremony/reception venue addresses, session preferences, and personalized notes.</li>
          <li><strong>Booking &amp; Financial Information:</strong> Payment transactions, deposits, and session agreements are processed securely through our verified third-party processors (such as Stripe and Pixieset Studio Manager). We do not directly store credit card numbers on our servers.</li>
          <li><strong>Technical &amp; Analytical Data:</strong> Anonymized usage data such as browser type, referring URLs, and interaction metrics gathered through privacy-compliant analytics tools to ensure our website performs smoothly.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>3. How We Use Your Information</h2>
        <p>We use the data collected strictly for photography business operations:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>To respond promptly to your session availability requests and custom pricing quotes.</li>
          <li>To prepare studio booking agreements, digital contracts, and invoicing.</li>
          <li>To coordinate logistics before and during your wedding, portrait session, or commercial shoot.</li>
          <li>To deliver digital photo galleries, print proofs, and physical albums.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>4. Image Rights &amp; Client Galleries</h2>
        <p>
          Photographs captured during your sessions are delivered via secure, private digital galleries. Selected photographs may be showcased in our portfolio, website galleries, or social media only in accordance with the terms outlined in your signed client agreement. We respect your privacy and will always honor specific non-disclosure or privacy requests agreed upon prior to your shoot.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>5. Information Sharing &amp; Third-Party Services</h2>
        <p>
          We <strong>never sell, rent, or trade</strong> your personal information to third parties. Information is only shared with trusted service providers essential to delivering our services:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Email &amp; Communication:</strong> Email routing providers for prompt inquiry alerts and confirmations.</li>
          <li><strong>Client Gallery &amp; Invoicing:</strong> Pixieset Studio Manager and Stripe for contract management and payment processing.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>6. Data Security</h2>
        <p>
          We implement rigorous security practices, including SSL encryption (HTTPS) across our entire website, to ensure your information remains protected from unauthorized access, alteration, or disclosure.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>7. Contact Us</h2>
        <p>
          If you have questions regarding this Privacy Policy or wish to review, update, or request deletion of your contact information, please reach out to Kimberly &amp; Rick directly:
        </p>
        <div class="legal-contact-box">
          <strong>K&amp;R Photography</strong><br />
          Kimberly &amp; Rick<br />
          Central Florida (Serving Orlando, Daytona Beach, Cocoa Beach &amp; Surrounding Areas)<br />
          Email: <a href="mailto:kimberly@kandrpix.com" class="legal-link">kimberly@kandrpix.com</a><br />
          Website: <a href="https://kandrpix.com" class="legal-link">kandrpix.com</a>
        </div>
      </section>

    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  .legal-page-header {
    background: #0D0C0B;
    padding: 140px 24px 70px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(184, 150, 53, 0.2);
    text-align: center;
    position: relative;
  }

  .legal-header-inner {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .legal-eyebrow {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 12px;
    font-family: 'Cinzel', serif;
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.22em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #D4AF37;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .legal-title {
    font-family: 'Cormorant Garamond', serif;
    font-size: clamp(38px, 5vw, 54px);
    font-weight: 300;
    color: #FAF8F5;
    line-height: 1.1;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  .legal-meta {
    font-size: 13.5px;
    color: #9C9488;
    font-family: 'Cinzel', serif;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  }

  .legal-body-container {
    background: #FAF8F5;
    padding: 80px 24px 100px;
  }

  .legal-content {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    color: #2D2824;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 16px;
  }

  .legal-section {
    margin-bottom: 48px;
  }

  .legal-section h2 {
    font-family: 'Cormorant Garamond', serif;
    font-size: 26px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #11100F;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(184, 150, 53, 0.2);
    padding-bottom: 8px;
  }

  .legal-section p {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
    color: #3D3934;
  }

  .legal-section ul {
    margin: 16px 0 20px 24px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 10px;
  }

  .legal-section li {
    color: #3D3934;
  }

  .legal-contact-box {
    background: #FFFFFF;
    border: 1px solid rgba(184, 150, 53, 0.25);
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 24px 28px;
    margin-top: 20px;
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    box-shadow: 0 4px 16px rgba(17, 16, 15, 0.04);
  }

  .legal-link {
    color: #A3802C;
    text-decoration: underline;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .legal-link:hover {
    color: #11100F;
  }
</style>
